flowchart TD
    A[Operation / Flow active] --> B{Failure or controlled negative outcome?}

    B -->|Controlled outcome| C[Reject / Defer / Cancel / Auth required / Unsupported]
    C --> D[Keep current canonical state]

    B -->|Failure| E[Capture failure evidence]
    E --> F[Owning responsibility classifies impact]

    F --> G{Was canonical target already committed?}

    G -->|No| H[Source state remains canonical]
    H --> I{Was actual platform partially mutated?}
    I -->|No| J[Fail operation safely]
    I -->|Yes| K[Rollback / reconcile source target]
    K --> L{Source/fallback verified?}
    L -->|Yes| M[Known safe source/fallback]
    L -->|No| N[Recovery Coordination]

    G -->|Yes| O[Handle as post-commit operational failure]
    O --> P{Can current state remain coherent?}
    P -->|Yes| Q[Degraded continuation / local recovery]
    P -->|No| N

    N --> R[Choose recovery target]
    R --> S[Apply recovery]
    S --> T[Read actual state]
    T --> U{Recovery verified?}
    U -->|Yes| V[Commit recovery result]
    U -->|No| W{Another automatic strategy?}
    W -->|Yes| R
    W -->|No| X[Manual recovery / support required]

    M --> Y[Observable final outcome]
    J --> Y
    Q --> Y
    V --> Y
    X --> Y

    Z1[User data integrity] -. priority .-> N
    Z2[Windows bootability/usability] -. priority .-> N
    Z3[Known coherent state] -. priority .-> N
